WEBVTT

00:00:08.547 --> 00:00:10.827
Quiet, musical hog! Knock it off!

00:00:11.107 --> 00:00:12.147
(SIGHS)

00:00:12.627 --> 00:00:13.867
(WHIMPERING)

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:16.987
Oh, Bullseye. I miss Woody, too.

00:00:19.187 --> 00:00:21.387
But he ain't ever comin' back.

00:00:23.547 --> 00:00:25.027
(SIGHS)

00:00:34.387 --> 00:00:35.747
(TOYS CHEERING)

00:00:38.027 --> 00:00:39.507
(TOYS LAUGHING)

00:00:43.187 --> 00:00:45.667
Rise and shine, campers!

00:00:45.747 --> 00:00:47.347
Commander Lotso, sir!

00:00:48.227 --> 00:00:49.667
All quiet, nothing to report.

00:00:49.747 --> 00:00:53.347
Excellent, Lightyear. Come on.
We need ya back at Star Command.

00:00:53.427 --> 00:00:55.747
Wait! What've you done
with my husband?

00:00:56.387 --> 00:00:57.427
Big Baby.

00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:04.267
MRS. POTATO HEAD: (GASPS)
Sweetheart!

00:01:04.547 --> 00:01:05.747
(GROANING)

00:01:05.827 --> 00:01:09.907
It was cold and dark. Nothing but sand
and a couple of Lincoln Logs.

00:01:10.427 --> 00:01:12.347
Uh, I don't think
those were Lincoln Logs.

00:01:12.427 --> 00:01:16.107
You all get ready.
You got a play-date with destiny!

00:01:16.587 --> 00:01:17.867
(RINGING)

00:01:17.947 --> 00:01:19.427
(ALL CHEERING)

00:01:46.147 --> 00:01:48.707
(CHILD SQUEALING)

00:02:10.507 --> 00:02:11.827
(CHILDREN SHRIEKING)

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:23.107
(CHATTER TELEPHONE RINGING)

00:02:38.147 --> 00:02:39.507
Uh, hello?

00:02:39.667 --> 00:02:41.347
CHATTER TELEPHONE: You shouldn't
have come back, cowboy.

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:45.787
They've cracked down hard since
you left. More guards, more patrols.

00:02:45.867 --> 00:02:48.027
You and your friends
ain't ever getting out of here now.

00:02:48.107 --> 00:02:49.347
I made it out once.

00:02:49.427 --> 00:02:52.267
You got lucky once. Want my advice?

00:02:52.387 --> 00:02:54.787
Keep your heads down. You'll survive.

00:02:54.867 --> 00:02:56.467
Yeah, for how long?

00:02:56.547 --> 00:02:57.707
I've been here years.

00:02:58.307 --> 00:03:00.227
They'll never break me.

00:03:00.347 --> 00:03:03.107
There's only one way
toys leave this place.

00:03:04.147 --> 00:03:06.707
Poor fella. Trash truck comes at dawn.

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:09.067
Then it's off to the dump.

00:03:09.507 --> 00:03:11.787
Look, I appreciate
your concern, old-timer.

00:03:11.907 --> 00:03:15.067
But we have a kid waiting for us.
Now, we're leaving.

00:03:15.147 --> 00:03:18.307
If you'd help us, one toy to another,
I'd sure be grateful.

00:03:18.387 --> 00:03:20.147
(SIGHING)

00:03:20.227 --> 00:03:22.627
Well, if you're gonna get out,

00:03:22.747 --> 00:03:24.467
first thing you gotta get through's
the doors.

00:03:25.067 --> 00:03:29.387
Locked, every night. Inside and out.
Keys are left on a hook in the office.

00:03:29.507 --> 00:03:30.467
WOODY: Got it. What else?

00:03:30.587 --> 00:03:32.747
CHATTER TELEPHONE: Lotso has
trucks patrolling all night long.

00:03:33.227 --> 00:03:35.147
Hallway, lobby, playground.

00:03:35.227 --> 00:03:36.427
WOODY: Yeah, yeah, yeah.
What about the wall?

00:03:36.507 --> 00:03:37.907
CHATTER TELEPHONE:
Eight-feet high.

00:03:38.027 --> 00:03:39.827
Cinder block. No way through it.

00:03:39.907 --> 00:03:41.187
You go over or under.

00:03:41.547 --> 00:03:43.387
That's it? Doesn't seem so bad.

00:03:43.507 --> 00:03:46.067
It's not.
Your real problem's the monkey.

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:49.987
The monkey's the eye in the sky.

00:03:50.107 --> 00:03:51.707
He sees everything.

00:03:52.547 --> 00:03:53.907
Classrooms.

00:03:56.707 --> 00:03:58.507
(SCREECHING)

00:04:04.787 --> 00:04:06.187
CHATTER TELEPHONE: Hallways.

00:04:11.187 --> 00:04:13.587
(MONKEY SCREECHING)

00:04:15.107 --> 00:04:16.747
CHATTER TELEPHONE:
Even the playground.

00:04:19.587 --> 00:04:21.427
(SCREECHING)

00:04:24.627 --> 00:04:28.427
You can unlock doors,
sneak past guards, climb the wall,

00:04:28.947 --> 00:04:32.147
but if you don't take out that monkey,
you ain't going nowhere.

00:04:32.747 --> 00:04:35.267
You wanna get out of here?
Get rid of that monkey!

00:04:35.347 --> 00:04:36.347
(BELL RINGING)

00:04:37.147 --> 00:04:39.107
Recess! Come on, kids!

00:04:41.307 --> 00:04:42.627
(GROANS)

00:04:42.707 --> 00:04:45.387
WOODY: Psst! Psst!

00:04:45.467 --> 00:04:46.627
Hey, guys.

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:49.107
-Woody?
-Woody!

00:04:49.467 --> 00:04:50.627
Woody!

00:04:51.067 --> 00:04:52.067
MR. POTATO HEAD:
Hey, hey, hey, buddy!

00:04:52.147 --> 00:04:53.387
MRS. POTATO HEAD:
Thank goodness!

00:04:53.507 --> 00:04:55.747
-SLINKY: You're alive!
-'Course I'm alive!

00:04:55.827 --> 00:04:56.907
(ALL LAUGHING)

00:04:56.987 --> 00:04:59.827
Hey, my hat! Wait, where's Buzz?

00:04:59.907 --> 00:05:01.587
Lotso did something to him!

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:03.747
He thinks he's a real
Space Ranger again.

00:05:03.827 --> 00:05:05.307
-Oh, no.
-HAMM: Oh, yes.

00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:07.307
Return of the astro-nut.

00:05:07.627 --> 00:05:12.147
Oh, Woody, we were wrong
to leave Andy. I was wrong.

00:05:12.467 --> 00:05:14.827
Jessie's right, Woody. She was wrong.

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:18.187
No, no, it's my fault
for leaving you guys.

00:05:18.267 --> 00:05:20.507
From now on, we stick together.

00:05:20.587 --> 00:05:22.347
But Andy's leavin' for college.

00:05:22.427 --> 00:05:24.267
College? Hog-tie the mailman!

00:05:24.347 --> 00:05:27.027
We gotta get you home
before Andy leaves tomorrow!

00:05:27.107 --> 00:05:28.627
Tomorrow? But that means...

00:05:28.707 --> 00:05:30.707
It means
we're busting out of here, tonight.

00:05:30.827 --> 00:05:33.667
-What? Impossible!
-But there's no way out of here!

00:05:34.027 --> 00:05:36.027
No, there is one way out.

00:05:36.627 --> 00:05:37.707
One way.

00:05:40.147 --> 00:05:42.027
Okay, here's what we're gonna do.

00:05:42.707 --> 00:05:44.627
(INAUDIBLE)

00:05:47.787 --> 00:05:49.667
KEN: Springy dog.
SLINKY: Present.

00:05:50.307 --> 00:05:51.787
-KEN: Green guys.
-(ALIENS SQUEAKING)

00:05:51.867 --> 00:05:54.067
KEN: Cowgirl.
JESSIE: Here.

00:05:54.507 --> 00:05:55.547
KEN: Horse.

00:05:55.667 --> 00:05:56.707
(BULLSEYE NEIGHING)

00:05:56.787 --> 00:05:58.227
-Piggy bank.
-Yo.

00:05:58.867 --> 00:06:00.507
KEN: Tyrannosaurus.
REX: Here.

00:06:01.187 --> 00:06:02.707
KEN: Barbie.
BARBIE: Here.

00:06:03.307 --> 00:06:04.667
Potato Head.

00:06:05.867 --> 00:06:07.227
Potato Head?

00:06:08.387 --> 00:06:11.187
Hey! Hey!
Tuberous root-man! Wake up!

00:06:12.187 --> 00:06:13.507
(GASPS) Impossible!

00:06:15.187 --> 00:06:16.227
Hey!

00:06:16.467 --> 00:06:17.707
(GASPS)

